{
 "header": [
  "SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0",
  "Copyright (C) 2026 Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>",
  "",
  "ISP overrides for the OV5647 NoIR module (no infrared cut filter) on",
  "L4T R35. Fitted to a ColorChecker on raw frames from a Xavier NX and",
  "an Orin Nano, under three LED sources and in daylight shade, and",
  "checked on the Xavier NX ISP output. Generated by",
  "tools/isp/make-override.py from camera_overrides_noir.json. See",
  "docs/isp-tuning.md.",
  "",
  "The white points carry an empirical correction of about R x1.08 and",
  "B x1.12, and source C was adjusted by hand, so that a grey comes out",
  "neutral on the ISP output indoors. The LED matrices have a saturation",
  "of 1.2 folded in. The daylight matrix is held weak, because infrared",
  "limits what it can do.",
  "",
  "Install:",
  "  sudo cp camera_overrides_noir.isp /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/camera_overrides.isp",
  "  sudo chmod 664 /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/camera_overrides.isp",
  "  sudo rm -f /var/nvidia/nvcam/settings/nvcam_cache_*.bin",
  "  sudo systemctl restart nvargus-daemon",
  "A line Argus rejects stops the camera, and journalctl -u nvargus-daemon",
  "names it. Matrices labelled 2000 and 12000 K stopped it without a log",
  "line. 2500 to 9000 K works."
 ],
